import{_ as t,o as i,c as n,a2 as a}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const g=JSON.parse(`{"title":"Entry 459 | Dragon Ball · Earth Setting Analysis: The Extreme Absence of Civilizational Construction","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 459 | Dragon Ball · Earth Setting Analysis: The Extreme Absence of Civilizational Construction","no":459,"module":2,"tags":["Myriad-Realms Benchmark","Dragon Ball","Earth","Civilizational Construction","Institutional Absence","Commoners' Situation"],"related":["03-Symbiotic Civilization Charter","36-Social Structure and Class Mobility","37-Symbiotic Education System"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0459_模块2-龙珠-地球设定分析-文明建设的极度缺失.md","filePath":"en/0459_模块2-龙珠-地球设定分析-文明建设的极度缺失.md"}`),o={name:"en/0459_模块2-龙珠-地球设定分析-文明建设的极度缺失.md"};function s(r,e,l,c,h,u){return i(),n("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[a('<h1 id="entry-459-dragon-ball-·-earth-setting-analysis-the-extreme-absence-of-civilizational-construction" tabindex="-1">Entry 459 | Dragon Ball · Earth Setting Analysis: The Extreme Absence of Civilizational Construction <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-459-dragon-ball-·-earth-setting-analysis-the-extreme-absence-of-civilizational-construction" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 459 | Dragon Ball · Earth Setting Analysis: The Extreme Absence of Civilizational Construction&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 2 · Myriad-Realms Benchmark Critique Library | Series: Dragon Ball Full Decomposition (Entry 28 · Civilization Analysis 1) | Benchmark base: Documents 03, 36, 37</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-a-planet-living-off-the-protagonist-s-protective-shield" tabindex="-1">Introduction: a planet living off the protagonist&#39;s protective shield <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-a-planet-living-off-the-protagonist-s-protective-shield" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: a planet living off the protagonist&#39;s protective shield&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Earth in Dragon Ball is the most familiar yet most alien planet: readers have followed Goku on it for forty years, yet know nothing of its government, law, education, medical care. It has Capsule Corp, Bulma&#39;s family, the World Tournament, but it has no parliament, no court, no civilizational institutional construction. It is a planet &quot;living off the protagonist&#39;s protective shield.&quot; This entry takes the republican axiom of Myriad Races as core, analyzing Dragon Ball Earth&#39;s civilizational construction absence.</p><p>This entry&#39;s judging base is the six top-level axioms and five mandatory cores, with the law-first axiom as core. The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning.</p><h2 id="i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" tabindex="-1">I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Earth&#39;s energy waste core is &quot;technology and combat power disconnected&quot;:</p><ul><li><strong>Technology single-pointed</strong>: Capsule Corp (Bulma&#39;s family) is Earth&#39;s only technology engine; Bulma stays home and Earth technology does not advance</li><li><strong>Combat power single-pointed</strong>: Earth&#39;s strongest combat power = Goku + Vegeta; ordinary cultivators&#39; highest = Gohan/Piccolo level</li><li><strong>Disconnect</strong>: Earth&#39;s technology (capsule spaceship, time machine) and combat power (ki cultivation) completely disconnected; technology not converted into a civilizational defense system</li></ul><h2 id="ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" tabindex="-1">II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression&quot;">​</a></h2><p>How Earth&#39;s civilizational construction absence feeds regression:</p><ol><li><strong>No government</strong>: Earth has no election, legislation, administration system; scatters after the World Tournament</li><li><strong>No education</strong>: Earth has no cultivation academy; Turtle School, Crane School are master-apprentice systems; knowledge not public</li><li><strong>No medical care</strong>: Earth has no public medical system; healing relies on Senzu beans (extremely low yield) or Bulma&#39;s healing devices</li><li><strong>No defense</strong>: Earth has no interstellar early warning, no defense system; Saiyans come and they hide; Cell comes and they watch</li><li><strong>Conclusion</strong>: Earth is not a civilization, it is &quot;Goku&#39;s training ground&quot;</li></ol><h2 id="iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" tabindex="-1">III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Goku&#39;s role in Earth&#39;s civilizational absence:</p><ul><li><strong>Accepting Earth has no institutions</strong>: Goku never pushes Earth to establish any institution; he defaults &quot;after fighting it&#39;s fine&quot;</li><li><strong>Treating Earth as training ground</strong>: Goku returns to Earth to cultivate and fight, not to build</li><li><strong>Senzu bean monopoly</strong>: Senzu beans held by Korin/Yajirobe, extremely low yield; Earthlings injured have no public medical care</li></ul><h2 id="iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" tabindex="-1">IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Dragon Ball Earth Absence</th><th>Anchor-Symbiosis Alternative</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>No government</td><td>Anchor Council + Symbiotic Executive Committee + Symbiotic Court separation of powers</td></tr><tr><td>No cultivation academy</td><td>300 Origin cultivation systems fully open; academified, textbook-ified</td></tr><tr><td>No public medical care</td><td>Symbiotic medical system (Doc 038); Myriad-Ranks medical universal benefit</td></tr><tr><td>No interstellar defense</td><td>Alaya Network + civilization-tier early warning; disasters have institutional response</td></tr><tr><td>Technology single-pointed</td><td>Joint contracting, more work more reward; technology engines diversified</td></tr><tr><td>Senzu bean monopoly</td><td>Life-cycle system (Doc 012) public; healing technology universal</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" tabindex="-1">V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li><strong>Modeling</strong>: Quest Sediment Domain replicates Dragon Ball Earth; inject Anchor-Symbiosis institutions</li><li><strong>Variables</strong>: stage — stage 1 build academies, stage 2 establish parliament, stage 3 build defense system</li><li><strong>Observation</strong>: count Earth per-capita combat power, commoner casualty rate, civilization survival years</li><li><strong>Review</strong>: output <em>Dragon Ball Earth Civilizational Construction Benefit Report</em>, quantifying &quot;turning Earth from Goku&#39;s training ground to Myriad Ranks&#39; home&quot; benefit</li></ol><h2 id="vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" tabindex="-1">VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Earth-setting self-consistency: low</strong> (Earth&#39;s technology level over forty years fluctuates high and low; Bulma builds whatever she wants)</li><li><strong>Civilizational construction self-consistency expected: high</strong> (after Anchor-Symbiosis injection, Earth has stable government, education, medical, defense)</li><li><strong>Retcon-ending risk: medium</strong> (Earth setting changes with plot need; GT&#39;s future Earth and Super&#39;s future Earth contradictory)</li><li><strong>Protagonist uniqueness dependency: high</strong> — Earth&#39;s survival hangs on Goku; no institutional backup</li></ul><p><strong>Old-new cosmos resource comparison</strong>: old-cosmos resources and Great Dao are finite, inevitably predatory involution; Anchor Symbiosis has everyone inherently possessing infinite origin, predation loses meaning.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: technology and combat power disconnected; energy not converted into civilizational infrastructure</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: Senzu bean monopoly, knowledge master-apprentice private transmission, Bulma&#39;s family monopolizing technology</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang Luo at least built Peerless Academy; Dragon Ball Earth does not even have an academy</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: Earth commoners under institutional absence have no self-organization ability at all</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: Earth cannot independently survive under Goku absence, let alone move toward interstellar republicanism</li><li><strong>Universal equal infinite law</strong>: basic infinite power inherent in all; easygoing retain guarantee, strivers can superimpose higher; infinite origin eliminates predation motive</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Dragon Ball Earth is a specimen of &quot;protagonist-protective-shield civilization&quot;: all its operation relies on Goku present; Goku absent and it collapses. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s answer is not to make Goku stronger, but to make Earth no longer need Goku alone. Let Earth have its own parliament, own academy, own medical care, own defense — let Earth from &quot;Goku&#39;s training ground&quot; become &quot;Myriad Ranks&#39; home&quot;; this is Dragon Ball Earth&#39;s true way out.</p><p>One more layer: Dragon Ball Earth&#39;s most absurd detail is — it experienced Saiyan invasion, Namek arc, Cell Game, Buu crisis, Beerus arrival, Tournament of Power; each time tens of millions died, but after battles cities build as usual, schools open as usual, economy runs as usual, as if nothing happened. This is not &quot;strong resilience,&quot; this is &quot;no true trauma.&quot; A civilization that truly experienced apocalyptic disaster leaves institutional reflection — establish early warning, reform education, improve medical care. Dragon Ball Earth left nothing, because the dead are revived, cities restored, reflection unnecessary. This is causal-self-discipline absence&#39;s fatal corrosion on civilizational construction.</p><p>In the final analysis, Dragon Ball · Earth setting analysis · the extreme absence of civilizational construction described in this document is no isolated case — its causality and energy-level traces are filed throughout in the Alaya Network, traceable and verifiable.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./460_模块2-龙珠-赛亚人设定-战斗民族的掠夺本质.html">Entry 460 · Saiyan Setting</a> · <a href="./464_模块2-龙珠-平民处境-普通人在战力世界的无助.html">Entry 464 · Commoners&#39; Situation</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/03-共生文明宪章.html">03-Symbiotic Civilization Charter</a></li><li>Official site: <a href="https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/</a></li></ul>',29)])])}const m=t(o,[["render",s]]);export{g as __pageData,m as default};
